{
  "name": "Broadcast Telegram messages to Google Sheets subscribers with rate limiting and blocked-user cleanup",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Broadcast Telegram messages to Google Sheets subscribers with rate limiting and blocked-user cleanup\n\n### Who's it for\nCreators, shops and communities that send updates through a Telegram bot. Telegram limits bots to about 30 messages a second, so looping over 2,000 subscribers in n8n hits 429 errors and some people never get the message.\n\n### How it works\n1. People send **/start** or **/stop** to your bot. The top lane saves them in the **Subscribers** tab and replies.\n2. To broadcast, add a row to the **Broadcasts** tab and set its Status to **Ready**. Every 15 minutes the middle lane picks it up, checks its length and marks it **Sending**.\n3. **Queue message for subscriber** hands one message per subscriber to [Jitterflow](https://jitterflow.io), which delivers them at a steady pace, with retries. The key `tg-<broadcast>-<chat>` means nobody gets a broadcast twice, even when a run repeats.\n4. The row is marked **Sent** with the subscriber count.\n5. Each morning, the bottom lane reads Jitterflow's dead-letter queue (DLQ), marks people who blocked the bot so they're skipped next time, and clears those entries.\n\n### Requirements\n- A Telegram bot token from @BotFather. Keep it private: anyone with it controls the bot. If it leaks, send **/revoke** to @BotFather, then paste the new token into the Jitterflow endpoint and the Telegram credential.\n- A Jitterflow account and API key. The free Developer plan works.\n- The `n8n-nodes-jitterflow` community node. It is verified by n8n, so it's available on n8n Cloud; on self-hosted n8n, install it from **Settings → Community Nodes**.\n\n### How to set up\n1. In Jitterflow, add an endpoint with the destination URL `https://api.telegram.org/bot<token>/sendMessage`, a pace of 5 a second or slower, and 2 retries.\n2. Select a Telegram credential with the same token on the trigger and the three reply nodes.\n3. Select a **Jitterflow API** credential on the three Jitterflow nodes and paste the endpoint key into **Endpoint Key**.\n4. Make a sheet with a **Subscribers** tab (Chat ID, Name, Username, Status, Subscribed at, Note) and a **Broadcasts** tab (Message, Status, Broadcast ID, Sent at, Note). Select it on all eight Google Sheets nodes, then activate.\n\n### How to customize\n- Edit the bot's replies in **Bot replies**.\n- Add `parse_mode: 'HTML'` to the payload to format messages.",
        "height": 1980,
        "width": 640
      },
      "id": "d4d4d4d4-0101-4000-8000-000000000101",
      "name": "Sticky Note - Overview",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [-420, 0]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## 1. Read the command\nEvery message to the bot arrives here. **Bot replies** keeps the chat ID and name, picks out the command and holds the reply texts, so you can reword them in one place.",
        "height": 800,
        "width": 640,
        "color": 7
      },
      "id": "d4d4d4d4-0102-4000-8000-000000000102",
      "name": "Sticky Note - Step 1",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [260, 0]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## 2. Save the subscriber, then reply\n**/start** adds the chat to **Subscribers** (or sets an existing row back to Subscribed). **/stop** sets it to Unsubscribed. Anything else gets a short help reply.",
        "height": 800,
        "width": 560,
        "color": 7
      },
      "id": "d4d4d4d4-0103-4000-8000-000000000103",
      "name": "Sticky Note - Step 2",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [920, 0]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## 3. Pick the next broadcast\nEvery 15 minutes, the first row in **Broadcasts** with Status **Ready** (or **Sending**, if an earlier run stopped halfway) is taken. One broadcast goes out per run.",
        "height": 540,
        "width": 820,
        "color": 7
      },
      "id": "d4d4d4d4-0104-4000-8000-000000000104",
      "name": "Sticky Note - Step 3",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [260, 860]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## 4. Check it and mark it Sending\nA message has to be 1 to 4,096 characters, Telegram's limit. A longer one is marked **Needs edit**. The broadcast ID set here keys every message it sends.",
        "height": 540,
        "width": 660,
        "color": 7
      },
      "id": "d4d4d4d4-0105-4000-8000-000000000105",
      "name": "Sticky Note - Step 4",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [1100, 860]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## 5. Queue one message per subscriber\nJitterflow accepts each message at once and delivers them at your endpoint's pace: at 5 a second, 2,000 subscribers take about 7 minutes. The row is then marked **Sent**. With no subscribers yet, the broadcast waits.",
        "height": 540,
        "width": 1040,
        "color": 7
      },
      "id": "d4d4d4d4-0106-4000-8000-000000000106",
      "name": "Sticky Note - Step 5",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [1780, 860]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## 6. Each morning, find chats that are gone\nMessages Telegram refused end up in Jitterflow's DLQ after their last retry. Only Telegram messages are kept, and only refusals that won't fix themselves: the bot was **blocked** (403) or the **chat was not found** (400).",
        "height": 520,
        "width": 860,
        "color": 7
      },
      "id": "d4d4d4d4-0107-4000-8000-000000000107",
      "name": "Sticky Note - Step 6",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [260, 1460]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## 7. Update the sheet and clear the entry\nThe subscriber's Status becomes **Blocked** or **Chat not found**, so later broadcasts skip them, and Telegram's reason goes in **Note**. Other failures stay in the DLQ for you to check.",
        "height": 520,
        "width": 580,
        "color": 7
      },
      "id": "d4d4d4d4-0108-4000-8000-000000000108",
      "name": "Sticky Note - Step 7",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [1140, 1460]
    },
